    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n45130" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">spontānĕus</span></b> , a,
		um, adj.
		sponte, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of one's free will</i>, <i>voluntary</i>, <i>spontaneous</i> (late Lat.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mors,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Macr. Somn. Scip. 2, 22</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">voluntas,</span>”
				<i>free will</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Cod. Just. 2, 3, 2</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">benignitates numinum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Arn. 3, p. 114</span></i>
			.—<i>Adv.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">spontānĕē</span></b> , <i>voluntarily</i>, <i>willingly</i>,
				<i>of one's own mind</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">apparere tumores,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Theod. Prisc. 1, 8</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Vulg. 1</span></i> Pet. 5, 2;
					<i><span class="en">Hier. Ep. 52</span></i>, n. 7.</div>
